s/issues/406","id":319424424,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMxOTQyNDQyNA==","user":{"login":"Mickael-van-der-Beek","id":4224802,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQyMjQ4MDI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4224802?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickael-van-der-Beek","html_url":"https://github.com/Mickael-van-der-Beek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickael-van-der-Beek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickael-van-der-Beek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickael-van-der-Beek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickael-van-der-Beek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickael-van-der-Beek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickael-van-der-Beek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickael-van-der-Beek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickael-van-der-Beek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickael-van-der-Beek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2017-08-01T16:30:57Z","updated_at":"2017-08-01T16:30:57Z","body":"Interestingly, the GraphQL endpoint for GitHub's APIs (https://developer.github.com/v4/explorer/) returns:\r\n\r\n```\r\n{\r\n  \"data\": null,\r\n  \"errors\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"message\": \"Fragment F0 contains an infinite loop\",\r\n      \"locations\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"line\": 12,\r\n          \"column\": 1\r\n        }\r\n      ]\r\n    }\r\n  ]\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nSo it seems they are using the Ruby GraphQL driver (https://github.com/rmosolgo/graphql-ruby/) which does check for infinite loops.\r\n\r\ncode: https://github.com/rmosolgo/graphql-ruby/blob/b8325f9767a2bab4abb6e93bfa33c3b883d3144d/lib/graphql/static_validation/rules/fragments_are_finite.rb#L12\r\nspec: https://github.com/rmosolgo/graphql-ruby/blob/aacf279b0503be80175